              "children": [
                {
                  "id": "lede",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Buying a new trailer is a major investment, and understanding the full cost upfront is key to making the right decision. It's not just about the price tag on the unit; it's about what goes into that number, what optional upgrades matter, and what long-term costs you should plan for. This guide will walk you through everything that impacts trailer cost so you can shop smarter and budget confidently.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full",
                    "anchor": "post-lede"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "h-new-trailer-cost",
                  "type": "heading",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "How Much Does a New Trailer Cost?",
                    "headingLevel": 2,
                    "align": "left",
                    "anchor": "new-trailer-cost"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-new-trailer-cost-1",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "The average cost of a <a href=\"/store/inventory?type=trailer&condition=new\">new commercial trailer</a> varies widely based on type, size, material, and features. The final cost can rise depending on what you need for your specific hauls. There are several key factors that determine the cost you'll see on the invoice.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "cards-new-trailer-cost-2",
                  "type": "card-lists",
                  "props": {
                    "variant": "stack",
                    "items": [
                      {
                        "title": "Trailer Size and Specs",
                        "points": [],
                        "intro": "Longer trailers and those with greater load capacity typically cost more due to the increased material and engineering involved."
                      },
                      {
                        "title": "Materials Used",
                        "points": [
                          {
                            "text": "Steel is strong and affordable, but it's also heavier."
                          },
                          {
                            "text": "Aluminum is lighter and more corrosion-resistant but comes at a higher price."
                          },
                          {
                            "text": "Combination builds balance cost and durability, offering a smart middle ground for budget-conscious buyers."
                          }
                        ]
                      },
                      {
                        "title": "Upgrades and Add-ons",
                        "points": [
                          {
                            "text": "Reinforced flooring"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": "Liftgates and ramps"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": "Air ride suspension"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": "Additional tie-downs or storage compartments"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": "Temperature control systems for reefers"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": "Toolboxes, winches, and backup camera systems"
                          }
                        ],
                        "intro": "These extras can quickly drive up cost, but may be essential depending on your business needs:",
                        "outro": "Every business has different needs, and the more customized your trailer is, the more you should expect to pay."
                      },
                      {
                        "title": "Manufacturer Reputation",
                        "points": [],
                        "intro": "Trailers from well-established brands often come with better materials and more thoughtful design, and warranties that protect your investment. At Sun State Trailers, we work with manufacturers that have proven reliability, so your purchase is backed by solid performance and support."
                      },
                      {
                        "title": "Warranties Matter",
                        "points": [],
                        "intro": "A comprehensive warranty may cost more upfront, but save money in the long run. It can cover defects in structure, components, and even electrical systems. Always ask what is and isn't covered before signing on the dotted line."
                      }
                    ]
                  },
                  "styles": {
                    "base": {
                      "marginBottom": 8
                    }
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-new-trailer-cost-3",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Ready to explore trailers that fit your needs and your budget? Browse our current lineup to find your next investment.",
                    "align": "left",
