                },
                {
                  "id": "h-ownership-costs",
                  "type": "heading",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Additional Ownership Costs to Consider",
                    "headingLevel": 2,
                    "align": "left",
                    "anchor": "ownership-costs"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-ownership-costs-1",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Sticker price isn't the whole story. There are long-term ownership costs that buyers should factor in to avoid budget surprises.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "h3-ownership-costs-2",
                  "type": "heading",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Maintenance and Repairs",
                    "headingLevel": 3,
                    "align": "left"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-ownership-costs-3",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Regular upkeep keeps your trailer road-ready. Plan for things like:",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "list-ownership-costs-4",
                  "type": "prose-list",
                  "props": {
                    "ordered": false,
                    "items": [
                      {
                        "text": "Brake and axle maintenance"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "Tire replacement"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "Lighting and electrical work"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "Reefer unit service (if applicable)"
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "cards-ownership-costs-5",
                  "type": "card-lists",
                  "props": {
                    "variant": "stack2",
                    "items": [
                      {
                        "title": "Insurance and Registration",
                        "points": [],
                        "intro": "Trailer insurance protects your equipment and liability. Costs vary by value, type, and location. Florida also requires registration and certain permits depending on load type."
                      },
                      {
                        "title": "Financing Costs",
                        "points": [],
                        "intro": "If you finance your trailer, interest will add to your total expense over time. Choosing the right loan term and rate makes a big difference."
                      },
                      {
                        "title": "Operational Downtime",
                        "points": [],
                        "intro": "Downtime due to repairs or poor trailer quality adds costs to your business. Investing in a dependable unit minimizes these interruptions and maximizes productivity."
                      },
                      {
                        "title": "Resale Value",
                        "points": [],
                        "intro": "Higher-quality trailers retain more value, which matters if you plan to sell or upgrade later. Investing more upfront may mean better ROI down the road."
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "h-pitfalls",
                  "type": "heading",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Common Pitfalls When Pricing Trailers",
                    "headingLevel": 2,
                    "align": "left",
                    "anchor": "pitfalls"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-pitfalls-1",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Avoiding a few common mistakes can save you thousands in the long run.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "checks-pitfalls-2",
                  "type": "check-list",
                  "props": {
                    "mark": "xdot-ink",
                    "items": [
                      {
                        "title": "Focusing Only on Upfront Cost",
                        "text": "The cheapest option isn't always the best value. Consider the total cost of ownership, including maintenance and downtime."
                      },
                      {
                        "title": "Skipping the Warranty",
                        "text": "Not all warranties are created equal. Make sure you understand coverage for the frame, components, and (for reefers) refrigeration unit."
                      },
                      {
                        "title": "Forgetting Compliance Needs",
                        "text": "Does your trailer meet DOT regulations for your route? Is it spec'd properly for your cargo type? Avoid fines and downtime by asking the right questions upfront."
                      },
                      {
                        "title": "Underestimating Load Requirements",
                        "text": "Purchasing a trailer with inadequate load capacity leads to wear, safety issues, and premature failure. Always match the trailer specs to your cargo profile."
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "h-faqs",
                  "type": "heading",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "FAQs About Trailer Cost",
                    "headingLevel": 2,
                    "align": "left",
                    "anchor": "faqs"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "questions-faqs-1",
                  "type": "qa-list",
                  "props": {
                    "items": [
                      {
                        "q": "Why do refrigerated trailers cost more?",
                        "a": "Reefers include insulated walls and a full refrigeration system, which significantly increases both manufacturing and long-term maintenance costs."
                      },
                      {
                        "q": "Is it cheaper to buy used?",
                        "a": "Used trailers cost less upfront but may come with hidden repair needs. Always weigh condition, age, and how long you plan to use the trailer."
                      },
                      {
                        "q": "Should I finance or pay in full?",
                        "a": "If your business has the cash flow, buying outright can save on interest. But financing offers flexibility and preserves capital for other investments."
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "h-shop-with-confidence-at",
                  "type": "heading",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Shop With Confidence at Sun State Trailers",
                    "headingLevel": 2,
                    "align": "left"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-shop-with-confidence-at-1",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Understanding what goes into trailer cost means fewer surprises and better long-term value. Whether you're hauling freight across Florida or expanding your fleet, <a href=\"/locations/trailer-sales\">Sun State Trailers</a> offers trusted equipment and honest support every step of the way. Find the right trailer for your business and budget today. We're here to help you get on the road with equipment that works as hard as you do.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
